Summary:
During today’s session, the focus was on learning basic networking concepts relevant to web development. Key topics such as IP addresses, DNS, HTTP/HTTPS protocols, and client-server architecture were studied. Attention was given to understanding how data is transferred between systems over a network. This helped in building a foundational understanding of how web applications communicate and function.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, there was a clearer understanding of fundamental networking concepts and their role in web development. The learning improved the ability to relate how frontend and backend systems interact over the internet. It also enhanced awareness of protocols and data transfer mechanisms. Overall, the session provided a strong base in networking essentials for application development.
